D -- THE SHARP VERSION.  Fastest saturation whose strong coupling stays above the Solar-System scale;
    the resulting boost ceiling against what galaxies require; and what the xi operator changes.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The Solar-System fluctuation the expansion must control is the scalar response to a PLANET on the
  background of the Sun's field: div[Sigma grad psi] = 4 pi G drho => delta_g = G M_p/(Sigma_eff R_p^2)
  at the planet's own surface.  Perturbativity needs delta_g << g_*.  Both shrink as Delta' -> 0; the
  RATIO is what decides.

